    "question": {
      ":question/id": "51c4f6aa-19b3-5088-bfb9-5d7134b50c0b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Differentiate $- 5 x\\tan x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=- 5 x$ and $v(x)=\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(- 5 x)'\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(- 5 x)\\cdot (\\tan{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(-5)(\\tan{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(- 5 x)(\\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=- 5 \\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(- 5 x \\sec^{2}{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
